Overlay patch 0021: SDL2 visionOS compatibility (Phase 1, VISION-PRO-GUIDE).
SDL 2.32.10 has zero visionOS awareness and its UIKit backend leans on
UIScreen/status-bar APIs that the xros SDK marks unavailable (90 compile
errors). This patch:
1. Adds cmake/dependencies/patches/sdl2-visionos-compat.patch to LUS — a
   ~25-hunk TARGET_OS_VISION-guarded port of the UIKit backend (virtual
   1920x1080@90 display replacing UIScreen enumeration; scene-sized
   UIWindow; traitCollection.displayScale for HIGHDPI; status-bar/launch-
   image/orientation machinery compiled out; 90 Hz CADisplayLink;
   SDL_PLATFORM_VISIONOS define for the backported sysurl guard). Inert on
   iOS/tvOS builds (TARGET_OS_VISION == 0).
2. Hunks LUS cmake/dependencies/ios.cmake to run it as the SDL2
   FetchContent PATCH_COMMAND via the existing git-patch.cmake mechanism
   (same pattern as the imgui/stormlib dep patches).
3. (2026-08-05) Carries the iOS input-forgery fix too — this is the ONLY
   SDL dependency patch wired into ios.cmake, so every SDL change rides in
   it whatever its subject. iOS/iPadOS synthesizes UIKit input from a
   connected game controller (B -> "cancel", A -> "select", d-pad ->
   arrows), and SDL's UIKit backend turned that into KEYBOARD events by two
   routes: -[SDL_uikitviewcontroller keyCommands] (UIKeyInputEscape) and
   -[SDL_uikitview scancodeFromPress:] (UIPressTypeMenu). The stray Escape
   made LUS toggle the SoH menu on every B press, through a path no in-game
   rebinding could reach (user report: GameSir X5 Lite, iPadOS 26.5). Both
   routes are now tvOS-only, where the Apple TV remote genuinely needs
   them. Nothing is lost on iOS: real keyboards deliver through GCKeyboard
   from iOS 14 on and the deployment target is 15.0 — and pressesBegan:
   was already skipped whenever a keyboard was connected, which is why an
   attached keyboard's Escape used to arrive twice (one route each) and
   cancel itself out.
Verified: libSDL2.a builds clean for PLATFORM=SIMULATOR_VISIONOS with
SDL_OPENGLES=OFF (GLES does not exist on visionOS; the Metal renderer is
the only one LUS uses).

